          "ruleId": "CWE-835",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "nanoid (Nano ID) before 5.1.16 contains an infinite loop in the custom ...\n\nnanoid (Nano ID) before 5.1.16 contains an infinite loop in the customAlphabet and nanoid functions of its non-secure module (nanoid/non-secure). When these functions are given a negative size, the loop counter is decremented from a negative value and never reaches its termination condition, spinning indefinitely and hanging the calling thread. An application that passes an unvalidated, attacker-controlled negative size to these functions is exposed to a denial-of-service condition."
          },
